        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "test(qa): redact script evidence diagnostics",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nQA script producers persist bounded child-process diagnostics as evidence. If stdout or stderr is tailed before redaction, a discarded prefix can remove the context required to recognize a credential while leaving its sensitive suffix in the saved artifact. Configured logging patterns can also span the shared redactor's normal internal chunk boundary.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis change keeps one redaction contract instead of introducing producer-specific secret APIs:\n\n- adds an internal full-context variant of the existing tool-payload redactor for callers that have already bounded raw input;\n- buffers QA evidence only up to a fixed safe limit, then redacts before taking the persisted tail;\n- omits oversized raw logs and failure details rather than truncating before redaction;\n- streams hosted-media and ClawHub child output into the evidence writer before their parsing/status buffers discard data;\n- retains the existing built-in and configured `logging.redactPatterns` behavior.\n\nThe regression crosses both child stream chunks and the shared redactor's 16 KiB boundary with a configured pattern.\n\n## User Impact\n\nThere is no product runtime behavior change. QA evidence remains bounded while avoiding secret-bearing tails caused by pre-redaction truncation.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/logging/redact.test.ts test/e2e/qa-lab/runtime/script-evidence.test.ts test/e2e/qa-lab/media/hosted-media-provider-live.test.ts test/e2e/qa-lab/plugins/clawhub-release-candidate-install.test.ts test/scripts/plugin-sdk-surface-report.test.ts` — 148 tests passed across two Vitest shards.\n- Blacksmith Testbox through Crabbox `tbx_01kwmw3czcxyb7qj0x5r1gvnn8` — changed type, lint, guard, and import-cycle checks passed; hydration run: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28682925039.\n- `test/scripts/plugin-sdk-surface-report.test.ts` passes after keeping the full-context option off the public callable export surface.\n- Codex autoreview of the final local patch — clean, no accepted/actionable findings (0.98 confidence).\n- Exact head: `dd0339fda57e7984a67f20dc48f82873b4278ca6`.\n\n",
